      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not only does it not work, it appears to make your audio global instead of obeying the \"Far\" setting. Any 2D (or partially) sound is also forced to be globally audible regardless of your settings. Please fix the VRC_SpatialAudio component!\nEdit: It appears that unchecking \"Enable Spatialization\" makes the custom falloff curve work. \"Use Audio Source Volume Curve\" is either broken or the VRC_SpatialAudio just sucks (seems like we need to use massive far values to hear anything if Spatialization is enabled??).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
